# CalHacks 13 — Real-time Space Event Photography Game

## Project overview

TypeScript monorepo for a real-time multiplayer game: players photograph real space events (ISS passes, launches, meteor showers) to earn points. Photos are scored with AI; event data is indexed for search/RAG; game state syncs in real time.

## Monorepo layout

- `/web` — Next.js + Tailwind frontend (player UI, camera capture, leaderboards); proxies photo uploads via `/api/sky-photo`
- `/sky_photo` — FastAPI service (OpenCV metrics + Astrometry.net plate-solve + vision judge + coded score + annotated overlay); not the Elastic event ingest
- `/ingest` — Node scripts that pull space-event data and index it into Elasticsearch (`@elastic/elasticsearch`)
- `/spacetime` — SpacetimeDB module (authoritative real-time game backend)
- `/lib` — shared packages (xAI Grok client via `ai` + `@ai-sdk/xai`)

## Hackathon tracks we are targeting

### SpaceXAI (Cursor + Grok)
- Build with **Cursor** as the primary IDE/agent workflow.
- Use **xAI Grok** via the AI SDK (`ai`, `@ai-sdk/xai`) for scoring, narration, and agent features.
- Integrate **Grok Imagine** and **Voice** APIs where they improve gameplay (e.g. event visualization, voice coaching during passes).
- Keep the shared Grok client in `/lib` so web and ingest reuse one configured provider.

### Elastic
- Index space-event catalogs and derived embeddings in **Elasticsearch Cloud Serverless**.
- Prefer **Jina embeddings** for semantic search over events, locations, and photo context.
- Use **Agent Builder** and **Workflows** on Elastic Cloud Serverless for ingestion, enrichment, and agentic retrieval — not one-off ad-hoc scripts when a Workflow fits.
- Config via `ELASTIC_URL` and `ELASTIC_API_KEY` (see `.env.example`).

### Spacetime
- **SpacetimeDB** is the real-time multiplayer backend (rooms, scores, presence, event windows).
- Module code lives in `/spacetime`; keep game truth there, not only in the Next.js API layer.
- Prefer SpacetimeDB subscriptions/reducers for live state over polling.

## Conventions

- TypeScript everywhere; Node >= 20.
- Secrets only in `.env` (never commit); copy from `.env.example`.
- Prefer small, composable modules; share types and AI clients through `/lib`.
- When adding features, call out which track(s) they strengthen (SpaceXAI / Elastic / Spacetime).
